# A fused pipeline: one loop, no intermediate Thread, no allocation.
#
# The `mod` is not decoration. Summing the squares up to twenty million
# overflows an int64, and the first version of this benchmark did exactly that
# — both languages wrapped identically, so the harness compared two wrong
# answers and agreed. `weave build -overflow` is what found it.
n is Source | strip | earth | otherwise 0

span 1 n | bend (x : mod (mul x x) 1000003) | sift even | sum
